<p>President Trump said U.S. and Nigerian forces killed Abu-Bilal al-Minuki, whom he described as the Islamic State group&#x27;s second-in-command globally, in a joint operation Friday in Nigeria. Trump said in a Truth Social post that he directed the mission and thanked Nigeria&#x27;s government for its partnership. Trump called al-Minuki &quot;the most active terrorist in the world&quot;. The exact location of the strike was not disclosed, and Nigerian authorities had not yet independently confirmed his death. The operation followed tension between Washington and Abuja after Trump accused Nigeria of persecuting Christians. The United States struck what it called militant bases in northwestern Nigeria on Christmas Day last year after those accusations.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/rDhVh4AYH_Q3oOoyBby6wFmVTleRu83vSYIdOqLd5sjFXYz1luG9ngT71I8VS99D21j57cyxe_TVK-5X76En8h6XgitbcLRZcQWTgDIeuFRG' alt='US President Donald Trump speaks to the press aboard Air Force One enroute to the US following his official visit with President Xi Jinping in China on May 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>U.S. designation: The United States designated al-Minuki a global terrorist in 2023, according to reports citing U.S. government records.</li><li>Operational role: A U.S. official said Washington viewed al-Minuki as a key figure in Islamic State organization and finance and believed he was plotting attacks against the United States and its interests.</li><li>West Africa link: The Counter Extremism Project said al-Minuki, born in Nigeria&#x27;s Borno province in 1982, led Islamic State&#x27;s West Africa branch after Mamman Nur was killed in 2018.</li><li>Regional base: The monitoring group said al-Minuki was based in the Sahel and was believed to have fought in Libya when Islamic State operated there more than a decade ago.</li></ul><blockquote>Abu-Bilal al-Minuki, second in command of ISIS globally, thought he could hide in Africa, but little did he know we had sources who kept us informed on what he was doing - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump said al-Minuki would no longer &quot;terrorize the people of Africa&quot; and that his death had &quot;greatly diminished&quot; Islamic State&#x27;s global operations. (<a href='https://www.infobae.com/america/mundo/2026/05/16/donald-trump-afirmo-que-las-fuerzas-de-eeuu-y-nigeria-eliminaron-a-abu-bilal-al-minuki-el-segundo-al-mando-de-isis/'>Infobae</a>, <a href='https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-05-16/trump-says-us-forces-nigeria-armed-forces-killed-isis-leader'>Bloomberg</a>)</li><li>Nigerian government: Nigeria&#x27;s government has denied Trump&#x27;s earlier allegation that Christians in the country were being persecuted. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/2000662/trump-says-isis-second-in-command-abu-bilal-al-minuki-eliminated'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/us-and-nigerian-forces-kill-islamic-states-second-in-command-trump-says/'>US and Nigerian forces kill Islamic State’s ‘second in command,’ Trump says</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/trump-says-isis-second-in-command-abu-bilal-al-minuki-eliminated'>Trump says ISIS No. 2 Abu-Bilal al-Minuki killed in Nigeria</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/2000662/trump-says-isis-second-in-command-abu-bilal-al-minuki-eliminated'>Trump says ISIS second in command Abu Bilal al-Minuki eliminated</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-says-isis-second-in-command-abu-bilal-al-minuki-eliminated/article70986019.ece'>Trump says ISIS second-in-command Abu-Bilal al-Minuki eliminated</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3353796/trump-says-isis-second-command-abu-bilal-eliminated-battlefield'>Trump says Isis second in command Abu-Bilal ‘eliminated from battlefield’</a> - scmp.com<